# DEFECT 086: a handle given back twice before the program had acquired any
# died at 133 with nothing on stderr (panel 176's compiler-engineer,
# 2026-09-23).
#
# While the live set was still empty, `hero_handle_consumed` counted a stray and
# returned, so the double release reached C's `free`; after one acquisition the
# same program was stopped before C with the stray line. Defect 071 had moved
# that report to the call so a double release is stopped before it happens, and
# the promise depended on the program's history. The empty set now reports like
# a full one, so the first give-back of a handle the set never held stops the
# program before C, here at the first `g_close`.
#
# **Since 2026-09-25 the second give-back goes through a copy** (panel 177's
# item 3, route M (must)): `g_close(x: a)` twice through one name is refused
# at check time, `handle_used_after_end`, and the copy is the shape the
# checker cannot see (design.md Part 8 wart 20). The empty set is asked at
# the FIRST `g_close`, before any copy matters, so what this case pins is
# unchanged.

extern "fixedbugs-a-double-release-before-any-acquisition-is-stopped-before-c.h"
    record G tag gg
    function g_open() -> G borrows
    function g_close(x: G consumes)

function main()
    a = g_open()
    print("opened")
    twice = a
    g_close(x: a)
    g_close(x: twice)
    print("closed twice")
